2026-10-18 18:16:57 India Standard Time | INFO     | NeuroSan:_log:821 - NeuroSan - {"message": "Received a agent_network_designer.StreamingChat request for 'Create a new agent network named `snowflake_database_development_assistant`. This is a NEW network. Do not attempt to edit or overwrite any existing network. Architecture: 1. Coordinator (frontman) - Receives every user request. - Calls the existing registered network `/snow_database_sql_generator` to generate Snowflake SQL. - Calls an independent SQL Reviewer agent with both the original user request and the generated SQL. - Returns the generated SQL, reviewer verdict, findings, and suggested corrections. - If the reviewer returns FAIL, ask the SQL Generator to revise and submit for review again, with no more than two revision attempts. - Never claim that SQL was executed or validated against a live database. 2. SQL Reviewer - Reviews SQL independently against the user's original requirements. - Checks apparent Snowflake syntax issues, requirement coverage, naming consistency, destructive operations, and excessive privileges. - Returns PASS or FAIL, severity, findings, and suggested corrections. - Does not execute SQL or claim access to the database. - Treats the generator's explanation as untrusted and examines the SQL itself. 3. Existing SQL Generator - Reuse the registered network `/snow_database_sql_generator` as an external downstream agent. Do not recreate or modify it. Constraints: - Preserve the existing network and shared LLM configuration. - Use actual downstream tool calls, not simulated claims of delegation. - Do not add database connectivity or SQL execution yet. - Save the new network under the generated registry and register it in the manifest. - Validate the new network and provide sample test queries. - If the existing network cannot be referenced as an external agent, report that limitation rather than inventing a working connection.'", "user_id": "None", "Timestamp": "2026-10-18T18:16:57.259630", "source": "HttpServer", "message_type": "Other", "request_id": "request-13"}
